James sought guidance on merging a specific file, "document.md," from a feature branch back into the main branch in Git, while leaving other commits untouched. I provided three solutions: the simplest method involves checking out the file directly from the feature branch into the main branch and committing that change without merging the entire branch. The second option is to cherry-pick specific commits affecting "document.md" for a more detailed history. The final suggestion entails merging into a temporary branch to isolate "document.md" before transferring it back to main. I recommended the first option for ease of automation and offered to assist further with Python scripting to streamline the process.
